{'symbol': 'SPGI', 'date': '2021-06-15 23:39:00', 'title': 'S&P GLOBAL PLATTS LAUNCHES CARBON-NEUTRAL LNG (CNL) ASSESSMENT', 'text': 'SINGAPORE, JUNE 15, 2021 /PRNEWSWIRE/ --\xa0S&P GLOBAL PLATTS ("PLATTS"), THE LEADING INDEPENDENT PROVIDER OF INFORMATION, ANALYTICS AND BENCHMARK PRICES FOR THE COMMODITIES AND ENERGY MARKETS, TODAY ANNOUNCED\xa0THE LAUNCH OF THE WORLD\'S FIRST DAILY CARBON-NEUTRAL LNG PRICE ASSESSMENT (CNL), WHICH TRACKS THE COST OF CARBON CREDITS PURCHASED AND RETIRED TO OFFSET THE CARBON EMISSIONS FOR AN LNG CARGO ON THE WORLD\'S MOST ACTIVE TRADE ROUTE. THE ASSESSMENT BRINGS TRANSPARENCY TO THIS GROWING PORTION OF THE LNG MARKET AS THE INDUSTRY SEEKS TO MITIGATE GREENHOUSE GAS (GHG) EMISSIONS AND DEPLOY FURTHER EFFORTS TO REDUCE THE CLIMATE IMPACT OF THEIR ACTIVITIES.'}{'symbol': 'SPGI', 'date': '2021-06-15 12:26:00', 'title': 'S&P/EXPERIAN CONSUMER CREDIT DEFAULT INDICES SHOW SECOND STRAIGHT DROP IN COMPOSITE RATE IN MAY 2021', 'text': 'NEW YORK, JUNE 15, 2021 /PRNEWSWIRE/ --\xa0S&P DOW JONES INDICES AND EXPERIAN RELEASED TODAY DATA THROUGH MAY 2021 FOR THE S&P/EXPERIAN CONSUMER CREDIT DEFAULT INDICES. THE INDICES REPRESENT A COMPREHENSIVE MEASURE OF CHANGES IN CONSUMER CREDIT DEFAULTS AND SHOW THAT THE COMPOSITE RATE WAS SIX BASIS POINTS LOWER AT 0.44%.'}{'symbol': 'SPGI', 'date': '2021-06-15 03:00:00', 'title': 'PLATTS LAUNCHES NATURE-BASED, HOUSEHOLD DEVICES CARBON CREDIT ASSESSMENTS', 'text': 'LONDON, JUNE 15, 2021 /PRNEWSWIRE/ -- S&P GLOBAL PLATTS, THE LEADING INDEPENDENT PROVIDER OF INFORMATION, ANALYTICS AND BENCHMARK PRICES FOR THE COMMODITIES AND ENERGY MARKETS, COMMENCED PUBLISHING DAILY CARBON CREDIT PRICE ASSESSMENTS THAT REFLECT NATURE-BASED CARBON CREDIT PROJECTS AND HOUSEHOLD DEVICE CARBON CREDIT PROJECTS ON JUNE 14, 2021. THE FIRST END-OF-DAY PRICES ASSESSED BY S&P GLOBAL PLATTS AS OF 16:30 LONDON WERE:\xa0 NATURE-BASED CARBON CREDIT PROJECTS\xa0– PLATTS CNC: $4.65 PER METRIC TON OF CO2-EQUIVALIENT ($/MTCO2E), REPRESENTING FIVE LOTS OF 1,000 CO2E UNITS EACH.'}